Navigation note: the web route /year-review/:year is a HIDDEN, deep-link-only route (web routeRegistry hidden:true; routeMeta maps it ->
/analytics for nav highlight). The Apple shell has no hidden-route mechanism, so a dedicated .yearReview AppRoute case was added (covenant
#7: the existing .analytics route + every sibling page stay hosted & untouched; .yearReview is NEW). Its pathSegment is "year-review", so
AppRouteParser's first-segment match resolves /year-review/2026 directly (IDs after the segment are tolerated) — no alias needed. The case
groups under Insights (mirroring routeMeta's /analytics parent). MenuCommandCatalog.navigateCommands() derives from AppRoute.allCases, so the
new case is auto-covered (testNavigateCommandsCoverEveryRoute stays green); the segment is unique (testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment stays
green); it resolves to its Insights group (testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup stays green). The web full-screen "story" (fixed inset-0 over app
chrome) is realised HIG-natively as an edge-to-edge dark story surface with its own progress bar / close / counter; the web navigate(-1)
close maps to an injected onExit shell hook (selection = .analytics), mirroring GlanceRouteRegistration's onOpenApp pattern.

